    "created_at": "2019-05-07T13:58:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-07T13:58:46Z",
    "body": "Even if we prevent `cache: reload` from being set by js I think the browser still needs to be able to set this value.  For example, if the browser is triggering a reload because of something like ctrl-shift-r, then I think the `FetchEvent.request.cache` value should reflect that.\r\n\r\nThis would make the value similar to `mode: navigate`.  Currently only the browser can set that mode, but its visible to script on `FetchEvent.request.mode`.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
