    "created_at": "2019-05-07T19:37:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-07T19:37:55Z",
    "body": "@wanderview: I agree! The change I was considering was related to the set of options that the `cache `attribute of the `RequestInit` argument to the `fetch()` API would accept, not to the underlying mechanism.\r\n\r\nIt might also be reasonable to allow CORS requests the ability to specify some of the alternative cache strategies, but we'd need to think through how they might allow attackers to evict cached resources they ought not have control over (e.g. evict only after a successful fetch?).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
