    "updated_at": "2019-05-08T14:27:09Z",
    "body": "Riffing on @yutakahirano's query parameters issue, if a response has a VARY header an attacker could request the url with a different set of matching request headers.  I believe most http caches only store one entry per URL, so this would evict the target url as well.  Kind of a corner case since it requires the response to use VARY, though.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
